Based on the compilation errors, I now understand:
1. `Point2d` is actually `CGAL::Point_2<CGAL::Epick>` (not the `cg3::Point2d` I assumed)
2. CGAL points don't have `.min()`/`.max()` methods
3. The `BoundingBox2` constructor expects different parameters

Here's the corrected implementation using CGAL's native operations:

```cpp
if (points.empty()) {
    return BoundingBox2();
}

double min_x = points[0].x();
double min_y = points[0].y();
double max_x = points[0].x();
double max_y = points[0].y();

for (const Point2d& p : points) {
    min_x = std::min(min_x, p.x());
    min_y = std::min(min_y, p.y());
    max_x = std::max(max_x, p.x());
    max_y = std::max(max_y, p.y());
}

return BoundingBox2(Point2d(min_x, min_y), Point2d(max_x, max_y));
```

